---
/**
 * QuestionnaireTiers.astro — V4
 *
 * Concentric-ring visualization of the v1 questionnaire architecture
 * specific to the agetech / Carestar case. The tiered structure was
 * doing two things at once that a flat list couldn't: collect enough
 * to make the forecast feel real, AND respect the limits of someone
 * already at their limit.
 *
 * Rings = required / high-value / enrichment, scaling outward.
 * The footer captures two parallel-architecture moves the rings can't
 * show on their own: conditional condition-specific subsets, and the
 * separate caregiver-layer questions that sat orthogonal to the
 * forecast inputs.
 *
 * Mobile collapses the diagram + legend to a single column and the
 * parallel footer becomes a stack.
 */
---

<figure class="v4-qt">
  <header class="v4-qt-head">
    <span class="v4-qt-eyebrow">v1 questionnaire architecture</span>
    <p class="v4-qt-tagline">A flat question list couldn't do two things at once. Tiers separated the goals.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="v4-qt-grid">
    <div class="v4-qt-diagram-wrap">
      <div class="v4-qt-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Three concentric rings labeled Tier 3, Tier 2, Tier 1 from outside in">
        <div class="v4-qt-ring v4-qt-ring-3">
          <span class="v4-qt-ring-label">Tier 3</span>
        </div>
        <div class="v4-qt-ring v4-qt-ring-2">
          <span class="v4-qt-ring-label">Tier 2</span>
        </div>
        <div class="v4-qt-ring v4-qt-ring-1">
          <span class="v4-qt-ring-label">Tier 1</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ol class="v4-qt-legend">
      <li>
        <span class="v4-qt-legend-num">1</span>
        <div class="v4-qt-legend-body">
          <h4>Required · every user</h4>
          <p>Care recipient relationship, age, U.S. state, primary condition. Geographic state mattered because care costs vary 3x across regions and the forecast was unusable without it.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="v4-qt-legend-num">2</span>
        <div class="v4-qt-legend-body">
          <h4>High-value · most users</h4>
          <p>Living arrangement, current help in place, recent changes in status. The questions that take a generic forecast and make it specific to <em>this</em> family.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="v4-qt-legend-num">3</span>
        <div class="v4-qt-legend-body">
          <h4>Enrichment · if willing to go deeper</h4>
          <p>Financial picture, family dynamics, what's working and what isn't. Optional. If answered, the artifact got meaningfully sharper.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <footer class="v4-qt-foot">
    <div class="v4-qt-parallel">
      <span class="v4-qt-parallel-label">Conditional subsets</span>
      <p>Diagnosis-specific question sets fired only when a Tier 1 condition was present (dementia, cancer, Parkinson's, heart disease, others). Putting clinical language in front of users whose loved one didn't have the condition would do more harm than good.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="v4-qt-parallel">
      <span class="v4-qt-parallel-label">Caregiver layer · orthogonal</span>
      <p>A separate set of personality and communication-style questions sat parallel to the forecast inputs and shaped how the GPT spoke to the user. Tone is a different problem than content.</p>
    </div>
  </footer>
</figure>

<style>
  .v4-qt {
    margin: 3rem 0;
    background: var(--cream, #F4EDE4);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold, #C8943E);
    padding: 1.75rem 1.75rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .v4-qt-head {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cream-deep, #EBE1D4);
  }
  .v4-qt-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, 'DM Mono', monospace);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-text, #8A6820);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .v4-qt-tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-display, 'Petrona', Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 18px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--charcoal, #2A2520);
    margin: 6px 0 0 0;
    max-width: none;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .v4-qt-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  /* ============ Diagram ============ */
  .v4-qt-diagram-wrap {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .v4-qt-diagram {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 320px;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
  }
  .v4-qt-ring {
    position: absolute;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-top: 14px;
  }
  .v4-qt-ring-3 {
    inset: 0;
    background: var(--warm-white, #FAF7F3);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--cream-deep, #EBE1D4);
  }
  .v4-qt-ring-2 {
    inset: 14%;
    background: var(--cream, #F4EDE4);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--cream-deep, #EBE1D4);
  }
  .v4-qt-ring-1 {
    inset: 32%;
    background: var(--gold-pale, #F0E4CC);
    border: 2px solid var(--gold, #C8943E);
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .v4-qt-ring-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, 'DM Mono', monospace);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--charcoal, #2A2520);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .v4-qt-ring-1 .v4-qt-ring-label {
    color: var(--gold-text, #8A6820);
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  /* ============ Legend ============ */
  .v4-qt-legend {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .v4-qt-legend > li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 36px 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .v4-qt-legend-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display, 'Petrona', Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--gold-text, #8A6820);
    line-height: 1;
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gold, #C8943E);
    padding-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .v4-qt-legend-body h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-display, 'Petrona', Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--charcoal, #2A2520);
    margin: 0 0 4px 0;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .v4-qt-legend-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'DM Sans', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--charcoal-mid, #4A443D);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .v4-qt-legend-body em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--charcoal, #2A2520);
  }

  /* ============ Parallel architecture footer ============ */
  .v4-qt-foot {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--cream-deep, #EBE1D4);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .v4-qt-parallel {
    background: var(--warm-white, #FAF7F3);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--charcoal, #2A2520);
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .v4-qt-parallel-label {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, 'DM Mono', monospace);
    font-size: 9.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--charcoal, #2A2520);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .v4-qt-parallel p {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'DM Sans', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--charcoal-mid, #4A443D);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .v4-qt-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    .v4-qt-diagram {
      max-width: 280px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .v4-qt-foot {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
